  "id": "ses",
  "term": "SES",
  "definition": "SES refers to socioeconomic status, a social concept used to describe a person’s or group’s social and economic position. Because it cannot be measured directly, it is usually estimated with indicators such as education, income, and employment, either for an individual or for the area where they live.",
